userStories.description:
**Goal** — Add the built-in post-run plugin that writes a per-run routing proposal artifact while leaving project routing config unchanged.

**Motivation** — The tool is advisory by default: the CLI writes config only with `--apply`; the plugin never writes config, only emits a proposal artifact.

**Approach** — `autoRoutePlugin` (`shouldRun` / `execute`) writing the proposal artifact, registered in `loader.ts`. The CLI and plugin are thin I/O shells that inject their external calls (`loadRunMetrics`, config write, artifact write) through a `_deps` object per `forbidden-patterns.md`, so their tests never read real metrics or write real config. Plugin fail-open — a failed calibration never fails the run: `execute` catches, logs via `ctx.logger` (write-only `PluginLogger`; no `console.*`, no emojis), and returns `{ success: true }`.

**Scope** — In: `src/plugins/builtin/auto-route/` implementation and tests, built-in loader registration, artifact writing to `routing-proposal.json`, `shouldRun` gating from `ctx.config.autoRoute`, and fail-open logging behavior. Out: writing `.nax/config.json`, CLI presentation, and any behavior that can fail the underlying run.

**Interface**
```typescript
interface IPostRunAction {
  shouldRun(context: PostRunContext): Promise<boolean>;
  execute(context: PostRunContext): Promise<PostRunActionResult>;
}
```
